{
  "name": "SQL2REST — Daily Product Export",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "cronExpression",
              "expression": "0 6 * * *"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "node-schedule",
      "name": "Schedule Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [0, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "http://YOUR-SERVER:8000/products",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendQuery": true,
        "queryParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "limit",
              "value": "500"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "id": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_CREDENTIAL_ID",
          "name": "SQL2REST API Key"
        }
      },
      "id": "node-get-products",
      "name": "Get Products",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [250, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "field-passthrough",
              "name": "product",
              "value": "={{ $json }}",
              "type": "object"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "node-destination",
      "name": "-> Google Sheets / CSV (connect your own)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [500, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## SQL2REST — Daily Product Export\n\n**Before running this workflow:**\n\n1. **Create a credential** in n8n:\n   - Go to Credentials -> New -> Header Auth\n   - Name it exactly: `SQL2REST API Key`\n   - Field \"Name\": `X-API-Key`\n   - Field \"Value\": your key from the SQL2REST API-Dashboard\n\n2. **Replace the base URL**: update `YOUR-SERVER:8000` in the \"Get Products\" node with your server address.\n\n3. **Reconnect the credential**: click the \"Get Products\" node, open the credential dropdown and select \"SQL2REST API Key\".\n\n4. **Connect a destination**: replace the last node with Google Sheets, a CSV Write node, or any storage target.\n\n**How it works:** Runs daily at 06:00, pulls up to 500 products. Increase `limit` or paginate for larger catalogs.\n\n**Self-hosted n8n on the same LAN:** `http://localhost:8000` or the LAN IP works fine.\n**n8n Cloud:** SQL2REST must be publicly reachable. See: https://sql2rest.com/docs/reverse-proxy/",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 450,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "node-note",
      "name": "Setup Instructions",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-50, -200]
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Schedule Trigger": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Get Products",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Get Products": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "-> Google Sheets / CSV (connect your own)",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "pinData": {},
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1"
  },
  "meta": {
    "instanceId": ""
  }
}
